From ad9ebd514b1dca525e0d3cfe2ab5e9102049abfd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:27:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] FP0105: report changes to state held in a field of the
 functional core

New rule, outside the AGENTS.md catalog, for the owner to keep or drop. Inside core it reports a write
whose chain goes back through access-path steps to a static field, an instance field of `this`, or a
get-only/init auto-property declared in source: element, indexer, field or property assignments and
ref/out arguments (at the target as written), mutating instance members of mutable BCL collections and
StringBuilder decided by the bound method's containing type (at the method name), and the static
System.Array writers (at the method name). Construction (constructors and initializers of the declaring
type), assigning the field itself, struct storage, reads, immutable collections, and chains rooted at
locals or parameters are not reported.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
